# The Hermes image builds use the repository root as their build context, so
# everything here is uploaded to the daemon before the first instruction runs.
# Only `upstream/hermes` and `toolchains/hermes` are ever COPYed, and the rest
# is either large, machine-local, or irrelevant to a cross build.

# Upstream checkouts other than Hermes. `upstream/defold` alone is far larger
# than the Hermes tree the images actually consume.
upstream/*
!upstream/hermes

# Git history of the Hermes checkout. It is a depth-1 detached checkout, so the
# object store carries no useful history and the image never reads it.
upstream/hermes/.git

node_modules
**/node_modules
build
dist
.git
.deherm
defold/.internal
defold/deherm
.DS_Store
.env
